# A5.1 optional local-API token (WAVR_LOCAL_TOKEN=auto persists the RAW shared
# secret beside the db as an extensionless `local_token` file -- NOT matched by
# *.db / wavr.db*). Never commit a live credential to this public AGPL repo.
local_token
**/local_token
backend/local_token

# tool-output dirs (never commit)
_fable/
.superpowers/

# F4 autostart runner logs -- backend stdout/stderr may pass through here; never commit
# to this public AGPL repo (wavr.db-wal PII-leak precedent).
logs/
# Root-level backend restart logs (may carry home-layout PII: camera/room names).
be_restart*.log
# Ad-hoc debug stdout/stderr captures (a manual verify run dumped real live YOLO
# camera-detection / occupancy data here — same PII class as the wavr.db-wal leak).
_debug_*.log
*_debug.log

# local competitive research — contains real home-network PII (subnet/hostnames/VPN IPs);
# keep OUT of this public repo until redacted (audit 2026-07-04)
docs/competitive-analysis/

# the user's real floor plan — home-layout PII, never publish (2026-07-05)
# F1: WAVR_HOUSE_MAP defaults to a bare cwd-relative "house.json"; the bare pattern
# already matches backend/house.json recursively, listed explicitly (wavr.db* style).
house.json
backend/house.json
council-report.md
docs/stack-netdoctor/
docs/feedback-sim/
docs/superpowers/

# roadmap stays local-only (private product direction)
docs/ROADMAP.md

# setuptools build artifacts. backend/build/lib/wavr/ holds a STALE duplicate of
# the whole package (old comments, old code) -- committing it to a public repo
# would publish a second, wrong copy of every module.
build/
backend/build/
*.egg-info/

# The bundled Core sidecar (PyInstaller output, ~40MB). BUILT, never committed:
# it is a generated binary, it would bloat a public repo, and CI produces it
# from desktop/sidecar/wavr-core.spec on every release.
desktop/src-tauri/binaries/
desktop/sidecar/dist/
desktop/sidecar/build/
*.guarantee-backup

# The dashboard packaged for the phone. Produced by
# `mobile/scripts/sync-frontend.mjs` from `frontend/`; committing it would
# mean the repository could no longer tell you whether the source still
# produces it.
mobile/www/

# ---- Signing material and machine-local paths, everywhere in the tree -------
# A per-module .gitignore only protects its own module. `mobile/android/` had
# these lines commented out (the Android Studio template ships them that way),
# and nothing covered the repository root or `mobile/` at all, so five of the
# seven paths checked were not ignored. Stated once, here, for every module
# present and every module added later.
#
# A leaked signing key cannot be un-leaked: whoever holds it can sign an APK
# that Android accepts as an update to this app.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
keystore.properties
local.properties
